# Testing Rules

> **TDD First**: For non-trivial features, follow `@.claude/rules/00-tdd.md` (RED → GREEN → REFACTOR)

## Backend Structure (pytest)
```
tests/
├── unit/          # Fast, isolated
├── integration/   # DB, external services
└── conftest.py    # Shared fixtures
```

## DO
- **Write test first** for new features (TDD)
- Name: `test_<module>.py`
- One assert per test (usually)
- Use `pytest.mark.asyncio` for async
- Mock external services
- Use factories for test data

## DON'T
- Implement before writing test (for non-trivial)
- Test implementation details
- Share state between tests
- Skip tests without reason
- Mock everything (test real DB in integration)

## TDD Quick Reference
```bash
# 1. Write failing test
pytest tests/unit/test_feature.py -v  # Should FAIL

# 2. Implement minimal solution
# 3. Run again
pytest tests/unit/test_feature.py -v  # Should PASS

# 4. Refactor, keep tests green
pytest -v  # All tests PASS
```

## Backend Example
```python
@pytest.mark.asyncio
async def test_create_session(db: AsyncSession):
    repo = ChatRepository(db)
    session = await repo.create(user_id=uuid4(), title="Test")
    assert session.title == "Test"
```

